; Two styles of one `@` font that select the same face, one of them bold.
; libass keeps whether a glyph's metrics are rotated by font, face, size and
; glyph, decided by the first lookup: the vertical comma the vert feature
; makes from 、 is first an advance lookup, so it stays horizontal in the
; regular style, also when ︑ maps it later; the bold style is another font,
; whose first lookup is through ︑, which rotates it.
